    {
      "id": "16aaa6ff-989d-4438-8490-01e2969c525c",
      "text": "On October 29, 2026, committing documentation in the active consumed engine worktree moved HEAD past the immutable consumer pin, and the existing checker correctly rejected the state. The selected remedy was to preserve docs commit/branch a918fbc, detach the active runtime checkout at 6d4ae39, and restore only the committed documentation/evidence paths; the exact-source checker then passed without reset, source deletion, repinning, or check relaxation. | When: October 29, 2026 | Involving: Project Madar engineering workflow | Identical package bytes do not permit a later documentation-only HEAD when the consumer pin is immutable. Future documentation commits must use a separate checkout or restore the consumed reviewed checkout before consumer checks.",
